    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0872" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1416: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T18:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Has the Paraguayan Government answered the notes sent to you by the
                    Department’s cables of October 3?<anchor n="89" xml:id="d618-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="0873" n="759" xml:id="pg759"/>
                <p>Department assumes from your 99, September 30, 8 p.m. and 101, October 7, 6
                        p.m.,<anchor n="90" xml:id="d618-f2"/> that Paraguay accepts to be
                    represented at the first meeting to consider the non-aggression pact on November
                    11.</p>
                <p>Has any indication been given regarding Paraguayan response to the suggestion of
                    the neutral representatives that forces in the Chaco be confined within the
                    limits of their respective forts? Affirmative answers to these two notes will be
                    very helpful at this time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
